        <mxCell id="legend_note" value="Note: WSM_Round_Robin_Group__c.WSM_Fallback_User__c, WSM_Round_Robin_Member__c.WSM_User__c and WSM_Assignment_Log__c.WSM_Assigned_User__c are Lookups to the standard User object, not shown here because it sits outside the package data model. Capacity Query and Capacity Filter arrived in v2.2: a Capacity Query counts records on any object the admin chooses, and its Filter children are the WHERE clause. Nothing in the package has a lookup TO those counted objects; the object and field names are held as text and resolved against the schema at run time." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=0;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;fontColor=#444353;fontSize=11;fontStyle=2;fontFamily=Helvetica;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1">
